From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:55:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/19] Add OSC 1337 SetUserVar

Programs can now attach variables to a session with the iTerm2 escape
sequence OSC 1337 ; SetUserVar=<name>=<base64 value>, which WezTerm and
kitty also support. Each change emits Session::userVarChanged, and the
variables can be read and set over D-Bus with userVar(), setUserVar()
and userVarNames().

Names are limited to letters, digits and -_+. ; invalid base64 is
ignored. A session holds at most 256 variables of up to 64 KiB each, so
a program cannot make Konsole hold unbounded data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
